  "body": "## What was wrong\n\nThe dashboard's automatic update/restart was aggressive: a hard-coded 5-second\ngraceful-shutdown budget force-cuts healthy long requests on every handoff, and\nthe supervisor had no defense against a held port, an incomplete runtime close,\nor a failed relaunch. On WSL this could leave the service unavailable or\napparently stuck on its port.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a bounded `Settings` field `SERVER_GRACEFUL_SHUTDOWN_SECONDS` (default\n  300s, range 1-600s) surfaced through the Limits page. The default sits just\n  over the measured p99.9 whole-request budget so most requests drain; the\n  dashboard reconnect budget is composed from install + drain + startup instead\n  of a fixed 120s.\n- Supervisor restart requests are now priority-ordered so a self-update\n  `REPLACE_PROCESS` cannot be downgraded by a later config-driven `RELOAD`.\n- Process replacement is refused loudly (logged + `SystemExit`) when the runtime\n  did not finish closing, instead of silently degrading to a clean stop.\n- `os.execv` is wrapped with a logged recovery command on launch failure.\n- Read-only port diagnostics (probe, bounded wait, `ss`/`netstat` owner lookup)\n  and a held-port gate before rebind; never kills an unrelated owner.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Targeted suite: 275 passed (`tests/cli/test_entrypoints.py`,\n  `tests/cli/test_port_diagnostics.py`, `tests/application/test_release_updates.py`,\n  `tests/config/test_admin_limits.py`, `tests/config/test_limit_bounds.py`).\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `ty check` clean on changed files.\n- Real-socket tests for the port probe/wait; supervisor behavior covered with\n  fakes against the documented uvicorn shutdown ordering.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- Dashboard surfacing of the refused-replacement state is not wired; the failure\n  is loud in the server log but not a structured admin message.\n- Real process replacement (`os.execv` swapping the running image) and the live\n  uvicorn drain under load are not exercised here.\n- Windows/WSL helper and `/mnt` behavior preserved but not re-executed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
