    },
    "message": "@\nfix(updater): graceful automatic update/process handoff (#80)\n\nReplace the aggressive fixed-5-second restart with a bounded, configurable\ngraceful shutdown budget so a self-update or reload never force-cuts healthy\nlong requests and the supervisor never leaves a half-serving port behind.\n\n- Add a bounded Settings field SERVER_GRACEFUL_SHUTDOWN_SECONDS (default\n  300s, range 1-600s) surfaced through the Limits page. The default sits just\n  over the measured p99.9 whole-request budget so most requests drain, while\n  the dashboard reconnect budget is composed from install + drain + startup\n  instead of a fixed 120s.\n- Make supervisor restart requests priority-ordered so a self-update\n  REPLACE_PROCESS cannot be downgraded by a later config-driven RELOAD.\n- Refuse process replacement loudly (log + SystemExit) when the runtime did\n  not finish closing, instead of silently degrading to a clean stop.\n- Wrap os.execv with a logged recovery command on launch failure.\n- Add read-only port diagnostics (probe, bounded wait, ss/netstat owner\n  lookup) and a held-port gate before rebind; never kills an unrelated owner.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n@",
